<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaocen ag Mohammed</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1880">1880</a>–<a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kaocen ag Mohammed was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a> leader of the Kel Ewey from the Aïr in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>. Linked to the Sanusi order, he led a major revolt against French rule in 1916–1917 and besieged the French garrison of Agadez for several months. After French reinforcements crushed the revolt he fled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fezzan">Fezzan</a>, where he was captured and hanged in 1919.</p></div>
